mission "The Bell Family's Passage"
    category "side"
    name "The Bell Family's Passage"
    description "Carry Elias Bell and his daughter from Port Royal to San Telmo, calling at Havana and Tortuga to collect the rest of their party."
    source "Port Royal"
    waypoint "Havana" "Collect Tomas Bell and his travelling trunk."
    waypoint "Tortuga" "Collect Maria Bell and two former shipmates."
    destination "San Telmo"
    reward 980
    to offer
        has "An Old Captain's Farewell"
    objective route
    speaker offer "Elias Bell"
    speaker waypoint_1 "Tomas Bell"
    speaker waypoint_2 "Maria Bell"
    speaker visit "Harbourmaster of San Telmo"
    speaker complete "Elias Bell"
    on offer
        conversation
            `Elias Bell, a broad-shouldered cooper with a worried expression, waits beside two travel chests. His daughter is studying the harbour while he speaks.`
            `"My family is scattered by work and bad luck, captain. We mean to settle in San Telmo, but I will not leave without the others. Tomas is in Havana. My daughter Maria is staying with friends in Tortuga, and two old shipmates have promised to join us there."`
            `He offers a careful purse. "Take us all the way to San Telmo. You must make the calls in order: Havana first, then Tortuga, and only then our new home. We will pay for the whole passage, not each little leg."`
            choice
                `"I'll take you all. Make ready to sail."`
                    accept
                `"I cannot promise that many harbour calls."`
                    close
    on accept
        log "Accepted The Bell Family's Passage. The required route is Port Royal → Havana → Tortuga → San Telmo. The two intermediate port calls must be made in order."
    on waypoint_1
        conversation
            `Tomas Bell is waiting on the Havana quay with a sea chest and a roll of cooper's tools. He checks the ship's name, then grins when he sees his father aboard.`
            `"I thought he might change his mind. Thank you for coming, captain. Tortuga next, then? My sister will be glad to see a familiar sail."`
    on waypoint_2
        conversation
            `Maria Bell stands beneath a striped awning in Tortuga. Two weathered sailors wait beside her with a pair of canvas bags.`
            `"At last! These are my father's old shipmates, Ben and Luis. They have been arguing about which of them knows the better route to San Telmo. I expect you will settle that before the day is out."`
            `The family is now together. Their chests and passengers are aboard; San Telmo is the final call.`
    on visit
        conversation
            `The harbourmaster of San Telmo checks the passenger list and waves the Bell family ashore. Elias counts the chests twice, then turns to you with visible relief.`
            `"You made every call and brought us here together. That is worth more than a fast passage. Let us settle the fare, captain."`
    on complete
        conversation
            `Elias pays the agreed fare and presses an additional purse into your hand. "A family is a cargo that cannot be replaced. You carried ours safely, and we will remember it."`
            `Tomas offers to repair a cracked rail on your ship the next time you call at San Telmo. Maria gives you a folded note with the names of three trustworthy chandlers along the southern route.`
        log "The Bell family reached San Telmo together. Tomas offered future ship repairs, and Maria shared a list of reliable chandlers."
